# DataCode local development environment.
#
# Copy to .env next to the Makefile:    cp .env.example .env
# Loaded automatically by scripts/dev-start.sh (and dev-backend.sh).
# Variables already set in your shell ALWAYS win over values in this file.
# .env is gitignored; this template is the committed documentation.
#
# The full configuration model (base + profiles, all env vars) is documented in
# doc/ops/configuration.md. Inspect the effective values with: make doctor

# ── PostgreSQL password — NOT set here any more ───────────────────────────
# The single source of truth is .data/postgres_password: created on first
# run (adopting the password a running postgres already accepts, or seeding
# the committed default for a fresh volume), read by every flow, and changed
# only via:  make pg-set-password PASSWORD=...
# A DB_PASSWORD set below (or exported) is used ONLY to seed/adopt that file
# on a machine where postgres runs outside Docker and its password cannot be
# probed — afterwards it is ignored (with a warning) whenever it disagrees.
#DB_PASSWORD=

# ── Recommended ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# LLM API key for agent-service — the global fallback that fills every model
# with an empty key. Without it every LLM call fails at runtime.
# Per-model overrides (naming scheme in conf/agent-service.yaml):
#   AGENT_SERVICE_LLM_API_KEY__DATABRICKS_GPT_5_4=...
#   AGENT_SERVICE_LLM_MODELS__0__API_KEY=...
AGENT_SERVICE_LLM_API_KEY=

# ── Optional ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Redis password — only if your local Redis uses requirepass (default: none).
#REDIS_PASSWORD=
